& [ObservedGap]
  + the P1 source permits bounded producer implementation but does not choose a race-free Windows process-containment primitive
  + ordinary std process spawn can execute before a job object is assigned and therefore cannot prove containment-before-first-instruction
  + closing or killing only the direct child does not prove descendant termination or descendant-free terminal state
  + current provider-free commission admission cannot authenticate itself acquire a lease persist one-use consumption or authorize execution
  + existing worktree preparation does not preallocate a durable production-broker ledger coordinate
  + current capacity below 15032385536 bytes independently forbids physical contact even after implementation exists

& [OfficialPlatformInputs]
  + Microsoft CreateProcessW documentation requires a mutable command line supplies explicit application environment current directory startup handles and process plus primary-thread handles
  + CREATE_SUSPENDED prevents the primary thread from running before containment assignment and ResumeThread must reduce the initial suspend count from one to zero
  + AssignProcessToJobObject applies job limits and ordinary descendants inherit the immediate job unless breakaway is enabled
  + JOB_OBJECT_LIMIT_KILL_ON_JOB_CLOSE terminates associated processes when the last job handle closes
  + QueryInformationJobObject exposes basic accounting including active and total process counts
  + Windows 8 and later nested-job support is required when the broker itself already belongs to an ancestor job; any invalid hierarchy or assignment refusal is terminal
  + pinned local windows-sys 0.61.2 bindings expose the required Foundation Pipes JobObjects Threading and FileSystem coordinates but no dependency version widening is implied

