& [WindowsChildContainment]
  + every manager-owned child uses CreateProcessW with an exact non-null application path mutable quoted command line explicit Unicode environment and exact current directory
  + each child is created with CREATE_SUSPENDED CREATE_UNICODE_ENVIRONMENT CREATE_NO_WINDOW and EXTENDED_STARTUPINFO_PRESENT
  + standard handles are anonymous pipes or exact null input and PROC_THREAD_ATTRIBUTE_HANDLE_LIST admits only the intended child-side handles
  + a fresh unnamed job object is configured before process creation with JOB_OBJECT_LIMIT_KILL_ON_JOB_CLOSE and without either breakaway flag
  + the suspended process is assigned to the job before ResumeThread and a resume result other than exactly one is terminal
  + version standard-schema experimental-schema and App Server are four exact sequential manager-owned children with no shell wrapper
  + version and schema jobs admit exactly one total process and zero active processes at terminal state
  + App Server job admits at most two simultaneous processes and at most four total processes for the server plus three sequential command children
  + timeout protocol fault output overflow assignment failure resume failure nonzero forbidden exit or late activity terminates the whole job and retains quarantine evidence
  + normal completion closes stdin waits within the exact deadline drains both output pipes queries zero active processes and only then closes process thread pipe and job handles
  + job closure remains the final kill fallback on every unwind or panic path

